  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is genomic infrastructure for non-model eukaryotes, mostly marine. Two preprints report primary de novo assemblies. The seep tubeworm Lamellibrachia satsuma draft (665 Mb, 6,320 scaffolds) was built from Oxford Nanopore and Illumina data and annotated. The red seaweed Furcellaria lumbricalis reference covers a species spanning saline NE Atlantic to brackish Baltic waters, which makes it relevant to salinity adaptation. Two NAR database papers operate at the clade level. PlanMine 4.0 adds new planarian genomes, 70 flatworm transcriptomes and expression resources. CoralDB integrates functional and evolutionary multi-omics data for stony corals. A secondary thread is noncoding RNA annotation by comparative genomics. CMfinder and R-scape analyses identify seven candidate structured ncRNA motifs in protists, some likely linked to photosynthesis. The aureoRNA atlas catalogs sRNAs and their predicted targets in Staphylococcus aureus.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
